#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0391 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "Authority: SEND Conformance Rules v5.0 SEND391 (SENDIG-DART 1.1/1.2), Rule 'DM.RPATHCD = TP.RPATHCD'; Plain Text: 'The value for RPATHCD for a USUBJID in Demographics (DM) should be identical to an RPATHCD defined in the Trial Repro Paths (TP) domain.' Declared Partially Executable (Overreporting), but the Source text and the Check coincide (phase-0 note); every DM row here populates RPATHCD, so no row depends on the populated-only reading. Row 2: subject S1-002 carries RPATHCD=F1F, a path TP does not define (TP has F0F, F0M) -> FIRES. Rows 1 and 3 carry TP paths -> silent. ALSO THE S3 FOREIGN-DISCRIMINATION PIN (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3): F1F exists only in the primary DM, so a port that read RPATHCD from DM instead of TP would find row 2's own value in its own set and fall silent."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=S1-002 RPATHCD=F1F
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SUBJID  type=Char label="Subject Identifier for the Study"
col SPECIES type=Char label="Species"
col SEX     type=Char label="Sex"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col RPATHCD type=Char label="Reproductive Path Code"
---
S1 | DM | S1-001 | 001 | RAT | F | 1 | F0F
S1 | DM | S1-002 | 002 | RAT | F | 1 | F1F
S1 | DM | S1-003 | 003 | RAT | M | 1 | F0M
---

dataset TP class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Paths"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RPATHCD  type=Char label="Reproductive Path Code"
col RPATH    type=Char label="Reproductive Path"
col TPSTGORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Repro Stage"
col RSTGCD   type=Char label="Repro Stage Code"
---
S1 | TP | F0F | F0 Female | 1 | PREMAT
S1 | TP | F0F | F0 Female | 2 | MAT
S1 | TP | F0M | F0 Male   | 1 | PREMAT
---
